HISTORY_VERSION 1.0.0

TYPE Governance

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-25

TITLE

Learning Protocol, Project-Management Standard and the Requests intake
added: PACE now learns from a correction once and stops re-asking.

WHY

The President stated two standing rules in one session. First: PACE must
have a place to learn from its errors and not repeat them — the AI should
not re-ask questions already answered, management patterns must be
permanently authorizable, and PACE should itself learn whether a lesson is
general to a project or general to the engine. Second: the ClickUp way of
working just used to stand up the PACE project must itself be part of
PACE's structure, created without deliberation each time. Both are exactly
the kind of permanent observation Vision point 6 anticipated.

DECISION

Created protocols/LEARNING_PROTOCOL_0.1.0.pdl: defines the intake (every
correction logged as a REQUEST before being acted on), the mandatory SCOPE
field (PACE / ORGANIZATION / PROJECT), the classification heuristic the AI
proposes and the ROOT_AUTHORITY confirms, promotion of an approved request
into a binding rule, and — the part that stops the re-asking — Handoff
loading of all approved rules at the start of every session.

Created standards/PROJECT_MANAGEMENT_STANDARD_0.1.0.pdl: fixes the ClickUp
shape every governed project takes (a folder per project; the lists
Roadmap/Fases, Backlog, En curso, Bugs, Hecho; the Roadmap seeded from the
project's own .pace/ roadmap), keeping .pace/ tool-agnostic while the
tracking convention lives at the organization level.

Created the top-level requests/ intake and logged the two founding
requests as the first real use of the mechanism: REQUEST-0001 (the
learning rule, SCOPE PACE, promoted to the Learning Protocol) and
REQUEST-0002 (the ClickUp structure, SCOPE ORGANIZATION, promoted to the
Project-Management Standard).

IMPACT

PACE now has a working knowledge-intake loop: an observation becomes a
REQUEST, is classified by scope, and once approved is promoted into a rule
that future AIs load automatically. This session is itself the first pass
through that loop. The ClickUp folder for PACE (space Pannotia) was created
the same session, matching the new standard.

NEXT_STEPS

Build the Bootstrap/Handoff engine that actually loads approved rules at
session start (the handoff/ folder is still reserved and empty). Wire the
Project-Management Standard into pace create / pace init so the ClickUp
folder and seeded Roadmap are produced automatically. Update the stale
README, which still says only the founding commit exists.

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
